    Industrial Networks: Network infrastructure specific to industrial operations
      Industrial Control Network Segments: Segregated network zones dedicated to control system communications
        ControlNet-A1: Primary process control network segment (192.168.1.0/24) for Unit 1 automation systems
        SafetyNet-S1: SIS network segment (192.168.10.0/24) for emergency shutdown systems
        ProcessNet-P1: Process network segment (192.168.20.0/24) for DCS operations
        DeviceNet-D1: Field device network (192.168.30.0/24) for instrumentation communication
        MasterNet-M1: Master control network (192.168.40.0/24) for supervisory systems
        BackupNet-B1: Redundant control network (192.168.50.0/24) for failover operations
        BatchNet-B2: Batch processing network (192.168.60.0/24) for recipe management
        UtilityNet-U1: Utility systems network (192.168.70.0/24) for auxiliary services
        DMZ-ICS1: Industrial DMZ segment (192.168.80.0/24) for data exchange
        MaintenanceNet-M2: Maintenance network segment (192.168.90.0/24) for engineering workstations
        TestNet-T1: Test environment network segment (192.168.100.0/24) for system validation
        QualityNet-Q1: Quality control network segment (192.168.110.0/24) for product testing systems
        ProductionNet-P2: Secondary production network (192.168.120.0/24) for Unit 2 operations
        LabNet-L1: Laboratory systems network (192.168.130.0/24) for process analysis
        StorageNet-S2: Storage systems network (192.168.140.0/24) for raw materials handling
        PackagingNet-P3: Packaging line network (192.168.150.0/24) for end-product handling
        EnergyNet-E1: Power management network (192.168.160.0/24) for energy distribution
        WaterNet-W1: Water treatment network (192.168.170.0/24) for utility processing
        LogisticsNet-L2: Material handling network (192.168.180.0/24) for automated transport
        EmergencyNet-E2: Emergency response network (192.168.190.0/24) for crisis management
        ClimateNet-C1: Environmental control network (192.168.200.0/24) for facility climate systems
        WasteNet-W2: Waste management network (192.168.210.0/24) for treatment operations
        SecurityNet-S3: Physical security control network (192.168.220.0/24) for access control systems
        CompressedAirNet-C2: Compressed air system network (192.168.230.0/24) for pneumatic controls
        ChillerNet-C3: Process cooling network (192.168.240.0/24) for temperature control
        LoadingNet-L3: Loading dock automation network (192.168.250.0/24) for shipping operations
        CalibrationNet-C4: Instrument calibration network (192.168.260.0/24) for metrology systems
        BoilerNet-B3: Steam generation network (192.168.270.0/24) for thermal systems
        FilterNet-F1: Filtration system network (192.168.280.0/24) for process separation
        VisualizationNet-V1: Process visualization network (192.168.290.0/24) for HMI systems
      Industrial Protocol Gateways: Network devices that translate between different industrial protocols
        Gateway-MB2EIP-01 (10.20.30.40): Modbus TCP to EtherNet/IP converter in Building A
        Gateway-PB2PN-02 (10.20.30.41): Profibus to PROFINET converter in Process Area 1
        Gateway-OPC-03 (10.20.30.42): OPC DA to OPC UA gateway for legacy system integration
        Gateway-BACnet-04 (10.20.30.43): BACnet/IP to Modbus gateway for HVAC systems
        Gateway-DNP3-05 (10.20.30.44): DNP3 to Modbus converter for power distribution
        Gateway-S7-06 (10.20.30.45): Siemens S7 to Modbus gateway in Assembly Line 2
        Gateway-FF-07 (10.20.30.46): Foundation Fieldbus to Ethernet gateway in Chemical Processing
        Gateway-ASCII-08 (10.20.30.47): Serial ASCII to Ethernet converter for legacy sensors
